      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(tencent): add Tencent Hy3 provider (TokenHub and TokenPlan)",
        "body": "Closes #99069\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nUsers on the `tencent` plugin could not reach the current-generation Hunyuan `hy3` model or the TokenPlan endpoint. The plugin only wired `hy3-preview` on TokenHub, so onboarding (`openclaw onboard --auth-choice ...`), the provider catalog, config resolution, and docs all had no path to the `hy3` model on either endpoint, or to the TokenPlan endpoint at all. Anyone with a `TENCENT_TOKENPLAN_API_KEY` or wanting `hy3` had no supported way to configure it.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nAdds a second provider id `tencent-tokenplan` alongside the existing `tencent-tokenhub`, expands the catalog, and wires auth / onboarding / reasoning-effort end-to-end so both endpoints are first-class:\r\n\r\n- Provider ids: `tencent-tokenhub` (existing), `tencent-tokenplan` (new)\r\n- Model catalog:\r\n  - `tencent-tokenhub`: `hy3-preview` (existing), `hy3` (new)\r\n  - `tencent-tokenplan`: `hy3`\r\n- Auth env vars: `TENCENT_TOKENHUB_API_KEY`, `TENCENT_TOKENPLAN_API_KEY`\r\n- Onboarding flags: `--auth-choice tencent-tokenhub-api-key`, `--auth-choice tencent-tokenplan-api-key`\r\n\r\nNon-goals: no core changes; TokenHub behavior for existing `hy3-preview` users is preserved (same env var, same onboarding flag, same default reasoning effort).\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\n- Users can now select `hy3` on TokenHub or TokenPlan via `openclaw onboard` and via `openclaw.json` config.\r\n- `TENCENT_TOKENPLAN_API_KEY` is recognized out of the box; no manual config surgery required.\r\n- Reasoning effort for `hy3` defaults to `high` and can be overridden to `none`; `hy3-preview` keeps its full `none` / `low` / `medium` / `high` range.\r\n- Existing `tencent-tokenhub` + `hy3-preview` users see no behavior change.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- `pnpm test:extension tencent` — 9/9 pass, including reasoning-effort injection for `hy3` (default `high`, override to `none` / `high`) and `hy3-preview` default behavior.\r\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions` — clean.\r\n- `pnpm test:extensions:package-boundary` — passes for all 116 plugins (tencent included).\r\n- `pnpm lint` — 0 warnings, 0 errors across `core` / `extensions` / `scripts` shards.\r\n\r\nDocs updated in the same commit:\r\n\r\n- `docs/providers/tencent.md` — provider table, auth env vars, reasoning-effort matrix\r\n- `docs/plugins/reference/tencent.md` — models / auth reference\r\n- `docs/providers/index.md`, `docs/plugins/plugin-inventory.md` — index entries\r\n",
        "branch": "feat/tencent-hy3-models",
